+    to it is translated as a whole, at the level of the loan, from its
+    [given_back_meta] (see [aloan_content_to_consumed_aux] and
+    [SymbolicToPureTypes.translate_back_nested_ty], which stops at the borrows
+    of the region group). The borrows of the abstraction's regions in that
+    value (the [given_back] side of the ended loan, one level deeper) end with
+    the region of the loan: the values given back to them are the values they
+    held when the loan ended, not inputs of a backward function. We bind the
+    values given back at [abs_level] to them (pure let-bindings emitted with
+    the next ones, see [bs_ctx.deferred_lets]): e.g., the value given back to
+    the inner borrow above is the value of [*s.0] when ['a] ends.
